{F} = \\mathcal{H}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-describe-pullback-pi-fppf}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{sites-lemma-mapping-property-glue}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{more-morphisms-lemma-dominate-fppf-etale-locally}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{lemma-proper-push-pull-fppf-etale}", "REF_0005": "\\ref{lemma-proper-push-pull-fppf-etale}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{proof}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0003": "\\noindent", "STRUCT_0004": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0005": "\\noindent", "STRUCT_0006": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0007": "\\noindent", "STRUCT_0008": "\\end{proof}"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:b192e67a68aaa38ac43cb9d8ac52553ce50eff900a7821154dd08fb56278dbad", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:be9849524272c774798c81db210c2330328c56afc365f6d35218d3c52af90214", "source_text": "<STRUCT_0001>\nThe functor <MATH_0001> is fully faithful (as <MATH_0002> by\nLemma <REF_0001>). Hence the forgetful functor\n<MATH_0003> identifies the\ncategory of triples with a full subcategory of <MATH_0004>.\nMoreover, the functor <MATH_0005> is fully faithful, hence the functor\nin the lemma is fully faithful as well.\n\n<STRUCT_0002><STRUCT_0003>\nSuppose that we have an <ACCENT_0001>tale covering <MATH_0006>.\nLet <MATH_0007> be the base change of <MATH_0008>.\nDenote <MATH_0009>.\nClaim: if the lemma is true for <MATH_0010> and <MATH_0011> for all <MATH_0012>, then\nthe lemma is true for <MATH_0013>. To see this, note that the given <ACCENT_0002>tale covering\ndetermines an <ACCENT_0003>tale covering of the final object in each of\nthe four sites <MATH_0014>.\nThus the category of sheaves is equivalent to the category of\nglueing data for this covering\n(Sites, Lemma <REF_0002>)\nin each of the four cases. A huge commutative diagram of\ncategories then finishes the proof of the claim. We omit the details.\nThe claim shows that we may work <ACCENT_0004>tale locally on <MATH_0015>.\n\n<STRUCT_0004><STRUCT_0005>\nNote that <MATH_0016> is an fppf covering. Working <ACCENT_0005>tale locally on <MATH_0017>,\nwe may assume there exists a morphism <MATH_0018> such that the composition\n<MATH_0019> is surjective finite locally free, see\nMore on Morphisms, Lemma\n<REF_0003>.\nClaim: if the lemma is true for <MATH_0020>, then it is true for <MATH_0021>.\nNamely, given a triple <MATH_0022>\nfor <MATH_0023>, we can pullback by <MATH_0024> to get a triple\n<MATH_0025>\nfor <MATH_0026>. A solution for this triple gives a sheaf\n<MATH_0027> on <MATH_0028> with <MATH_0029>.\nBy the first paragraph of the proof this means the triple is\nin the essential image. This reduces us to\nthe case described in the next paragraph.\n\n<STRUCT_0006><STRUCT_0007>\nAssume <MATH_0030> is surjective finite locally free.\nLet <MATH_0031> be a triple.\nIn this case consider the triple\n<MATH_0032>\nwhere <MATH_0033> comes from the identifications\n<MATH_0034>\nwhere the third equality is Lemma <REF_0004>\nand the arrow is given by <MATH_0035>.\nThis triple is in the image of our functor because\n<MATH_0036> is a solution\n(to see this use Lemma <REF_0005> again;\ndetails omitted). There is a canonical map of triples\n<MATH_0037>\nwhich uses the unit <MATH_0038>\non the second entry (it is enough to prescribe morphisms on the\nsecond entry by the first paragraph of the proof). Since\n<MATH_0039> is an fppf covering the map\n<MATH_0040> is injective (details omitted).\nSet\n<MATH_0041>\nand let <MATH_0042> be the induced isomorphism (pullback functors\nare exact, so this makes sense). Then <MATH_0043> is the\nequalizer of the two maps <MATH_0044>.\nRepeating the arguments above for the triple\n<MATH_0045>\nwe find an injective morphism of triples\n<MATH_0046>\nsuch that this last triple is in the image of our functor.\nSay it corresponds to <MATH_0047> in <MATH_0048>.\nBy fully faithfulness we obtain two maps\n<MATH_0049> and we can let\n<MATH_0050> be the equalizer of these two maps.\nBy exactness of the pullback functors involved we\nfind that <MATH_0051> as desired.\n<STRUCT_0008>", "source_text_hash": "sha256:20e0f44ef77baaf2d414ecb7b99097971c43b4b230e1ee501a267130c1b9b470", "unit_id": "inventory:etale-cohomology:0DEU:proof/0001"}}}, {"context_id": "locked-English-reference:etale-cohomology:inventory:etale-cohomology:0DDM:lemma/0001:etale-cohomology-lemma-push-pull-fppf-etale", "hash": "sha256:8bf972e99c9a32b437392158ae3d099e3302314690b29ef406ef7956f2a991de", "value": {"kind": "locked-English-reference", "location": {"byte_end": 805292, "byte_start": 804659, "file": "etale-cohomology.tex", "fragment_hash": "sha256:11683058a3e5843708e025bb2159beac9241792cace629f0dbcf060de460a569", "line_end": 21506, "line_start": 21483}, "owner_tag": "0DDM", "parent_tag": "0DDK", "requested_label": "etale-cohomology-lemma-push-pull-fppf-etale", "requested_tag": "0DDM", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_unit": {"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "0DDK", "placeholders": {"LOCKED_0001": "\\label{lemma-push-pull-fppf-etale}", "MATH_0001": "$f : X \\to Y$", "MATH_0002": "$(\\Sch/S)_{fppf}$", "MATH_0003": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\n\\Sh((\\Sch/X)_{fppf}) \\ar[rr]_{f_{big, fppf}} \\ar[d]_{\\epsilon_X} & &\n\\Sh((\\Sch/Y)_{fppf}) \\ar[d]^{\\epsilon_Y} \\\\\n\\Sh((\\Sch/X)_\\etale) \\ar[rr]^{f_{big, \\etale}} & &\n\\Sh((\\Sch/Y)_\\etale)\n}\n$$", "MATH_0004": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\n\\Sh((\\Sch/X)_{fppf}) \\ar[rr]_{f_{big, fppf}} \\ar[d]_{a_X} & &\n\\Sh((\\Sch/Y)_{fppf}) \\ar[d]^{a_Y} \\\\\n\\Sh(X_\\etale) \\ar[rr]^{f_{small}} & &\n\\Sh(Y_\\etale)\n}\n$$", "MATH_0005": "$a_X = \\pi_X \\circ \\epsilon_X$", "MATH_0006": "$a_Y = \\pi_X \\circ \\epsilon_X$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{lemma}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\end{lemma}"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_ha